      {
        "id": 2124306913,
        "content": "Resolves #331\r\nI've refactored the codebase to have a single responsibility point for managing buttons visibility. The reason why a lot of glitches happened previously was that there were a lot of functions managing the buttons state. There were also a lot of nested network verification code something like: verify-current-network.ts -> handle-if-on-correct-network.ts -> not-in-correct-network.ts and so on. They would all have the same purpose but would delegate the job to the next one, so I've unified that as well. We have a single function that is called on load and on `window.ethereum` events.\r\nHere is a video showing all scenarios:\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0e15a97-b34f-452e-bd88-2ee0582f4306",
